{"resourceIdentifier":"674","resourceName":"Rimba Raya Biodiversity Reserve Project","description":"The Rimba Raya Biodiversity Reserve Project, an initiative by InfiniteEARTH, aims to reduce Indonesia’s emissions by preserving some 64,000 hectares of tropical peat swamp forest. This area, rich in biodiversity including the endangered Bornean orangutan, was slated by the Provincial government to be converted into four palm oil estates. Located on the southern coast of Borneo in the province of Central Kalimantan, the project is also designed to protect the integrity of the adjacent world-renowned Tanjung Puting National Park, by creating a physical buffer zone on the full extent of the ~90km eastern border of the park.","location":{"latitude":-3.106367,"longitude":112.299244},"inPublicCommentPeriod":false,"lastPublicCommentPeriod":{"startInclusive":"2022-05-04","endExclusive":"2022-06-04","endInclusive":"2022-06-03"},"attributes":[{"code":"PROJECT_ID","values":[{"type":"string","value":"674"}]},{"code":"STATE_PROVINCE","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Central Kalimantan"}]}],"participationSummaries":[{"programCode":"VCS","attributes":[{"code":"PROPONENT_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"InfiniteEARTH"},{"type":"string","value":"Hong Kong, Hong Kong"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_STATUS","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Late to verify"},{"type":"assetSearchLink","value":null,"targetId":"674"},{"type":"bufferSearchLink","value":null,"targetId":"674"}]},{"code":"EST_ANNUAL_EMISSION_REDCT","values":[{"type":"string","value":"3527171"}]},{"code":"TOTAL_BUFFER_POOL_CREDITS","values":[{"type":"integer","value":3838689}]},{"code":"PRIMARY_PROJECT_CATEGORY_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Agriculture Forestry and Other Land Use"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_SUBCATERGORY_NAMES","values":[{"type":"string","value":"REDD"}]},{"code":"PROTOCOL_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"VM0004"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_ACREAGE","values":[{"type":"string","value":"64977 Hectares"}]},